 We present Agentic RISC (Risk-Bounded Intent, Scope and Control), an implementation-neutral framework for institution-owned authority, shared accounting, enforceable execution boundaries, and reconciliation from accepted outcomes. Its Action Contract links a proposed effect to authorization, any required reservation, executable authority, and outcome evidence. A RISC Runtime maintains the authority book; a RISC Gateway enforces it at the protected effect boundary. The objective is broader delegation without allowing models, harnesses, or child agents to enlarge their own mandate.
 
