 \subsection{Safety needs an operational recovery path}
 Holding unresolved commitments can strand capacity. Within one fixed accounting window, a missing response can leave two histories indistinguishable: the action never executed and cannot execute, or it executed but its receipt is missing. A deadline alone cannot tell the Runtime which history occurred. Reuse may be unsafe in the second; withholding may reduce availability in the first. An authoritative outcome query, confirmed cancellation, or atomic non-use closure can supply the missing distinction.
